# Security hygiene

Adapted lightly from awesome-cursorrules DevSecOps rule; scoped to this
research codebase (no web auth stack).

- Never commit `.env`, API tokens, Hugging Face tokens, or credentials.
- Do not print secrets in logs or inspection reports.
- Keep downloads and caches under `$MBS_*` roots on `/data`.
- Do not weaken path guards that require artifacts under `/data`.
- Prefer pinning and reviewing `vendor/` via `SOURCES.lock.yaml`; do not
  silently vendor unpinned third-party code into `src/`.
- When reviewing PRs or diffs, flag secret leaks, path escapes, and unvalidated
  deserialization of untrusted pickles/checkpoints.
